  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "The M with a bonus – stay alert after the shot",
  "description": "A follow-on from the M. Two lines in the corners at one end and a cone on each side further out. A skates down and around their cone, gets a diagonal pass from B in the other corner and shoots – first time or after a touch.\n\nAfter the shot, A turns towards their own corner, gets a pass from the first player there (C) and plays it straight back. C then plays the diagonal pass to B, who has gone around their cone in the meantime. And so it rolls on.\n\nIt is easy to switch off after a shot. Here the players learn to stay alert after it too. Swap lines so everyone shoots from both sides. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Do not switch off after the shot – turn towards your corner straight away."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The first-time pass back should be firm and accurate."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The skater shows with the stick where they want the puck."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 2,
  "focus": [
